# Config & Deployment — Security Rules

Applies to `app/config/`, `index.php`, `.htaccess`.

## Secrets — Never Commit

| Item | Location | Rule |
|------|----------|------|
| DB password | `database.php` | Local dev only; warn if pushing real prod creds |
| `encryption_key` | `config.php` | Must be long/random; never empty in prod |
| Stripe/PayPal keys | `payment_gateways.php` | Test keys in dev; prod via secure deploy |
| OAuth secrets | `google_config.php`, `facebook.php` | Empty in repo; fill per environment |

**Agent:** If diff adds/changes secrets → warn user before commit.

## Production Settings (verify before go-live)

| Setting | File | Production |
|---------|------|--------------|
| `ENVIRONMENT` | `index.php` | `production` |
| `db_debug` | `database.php` | `FALSE` |
| `display_errors` | `index.php` | off |
| `log_threshold` | `config.php` | log errors; no display to user |
| `csrf_protection` | `config.php` | `TRUE` |

## CSRF

- `csrf_exclude_uris` — **minimal list only** (payment IPN, webhooks, external callbacks).
- Do not add URIs to exclude without PM approval.
- New forms/AJAX POSTs must include CSRF token per CI pattern.

## Multi-Tenant (`database.php`)

- Subdomain routing logic — **do not alter** (upgrade rule).
- No SQL injection via `HTTP_HOST` — subdomain must be validated/sanitized if used in queries.

## `.htaccess` / Entry

- Do not expose `app/`, `system/`, `vendor/` directly.
- `index.php` front controller only.

## Session & Cookies

- `cookie_secure` → TRUE when HTTPS in production.
- `cookie_httponly` → TRUE.
- Session path under `application/cache/` or configured path — not world-writable.

